abstract: >
  The Chess Multiverse Error & Evaluation Dataset (CMEED v1.0) is a
  large-scale open-source chess research dataset containing structured
  human decision-making errors extracted from official chess broadcasts.
  The dataset includes engine-annotated inaccuracies, mistakes, and
  blunders together with player metadata, opening information, engine
  evaluations, evaluation swings, clock information, move details, and
  fully reconstructed board positions represented as FEN strings before
  and after each error move. CMEED v1.0 contains 994,269 error records
  extracted from 106,911 games played between January 2026 and May 2026.
  The dataset is designed to support chess analytics, human error
  modeling, machine learning, decision-making research, sports
  analytics, cognitive science, and large-scale statistical studies of
  human chess performance.
